BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Kilnbright) Tj T* () Tj T* (Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Kilnbright) Tj T* (A Smart Kiln Controller for Classroom Learning) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (In middle schools across America, art teachers have a problem with kilns. Kilns is very hot, up) Tj T* (to over two thousand degrees, and are danger if the teacher do not know how to use it correct.) Tj T* (Many teachers are not trained for firing ceramics and they are afraid of the kiln so some) Tj T* (schools dont even use there kiln at all and it sit in the corner. This is a big problem because) Tj T* (ceramics is a important part of art education and students loses the chance to make things with) Tj T* (there hands. Also the old kiln controllers is hard to understand with many buttons and numbers) Tj T* (and codes that the teacher must learn. When the teacher make mistake the pottery can break or) Tj T* (explode and this waste time and money and the students feels bad. Also the students do not) Tj T* (learn nothing about the science of heat during firing, which is a missed opportunity in STEM) Tj T* (education. We think this problem is very big and it need to be solved.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Kilnbright is the solution. It is a low cost digital kiln controller that is classroom safe.) Tj T* (The teacher just plug it into the kiln and choose a preset program like bisque or glaze and) Tj T* (push the button. Then Kilnbright do everything automatic and the teacher dont need to) Tj T* (understand the temperatures. It have a safety feature that shut off the kiln if it get too hot.) Tj T* (It also have a color screen who show the students what is happening inside the kiln and explain) Tj T* (the science of heat and glaze chemistry in a fun way. So Kilnbright is both a controller and a) Tj T* (education tool. We believe this is a innovative and disruptive solution that will change how) Tj T* (ceramics is taught. Our controller is easy, safe, smart, and fun, and it is the first to) Tj T* (combine all of these things together in one product for schools.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (The market for Kilnbright is very large. There is thousands of middle schools in the United) Tj T* (States and each one have a art teacher and many have a kiln. Education is a huge market worth) Tj T* (billions of dollars and technology in education is growing every year. If we get only one) Tj T* (percent of the market we will make a lot of money. Also there is private art studios, summer) Tj T* (camps, community centers, and hobby potters who might want our product too, so the market is) Tj T* (even bigger. We think the total market is over one billion dollars. Schools are always looking) Tj T* (for new STEM products because of the focus on STEM in education and the government give funding) Tj T* (for it. Teachers also buy things themselves with there own money for the classroom. The market) Tj T* (is growing and our timing is perfect because everybody is talking about STEM and hands on) Tj T* (learning right now.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We will make money by selling the Kilnbright controller to schools and teachers. The price will) Tj T* (be about two hundred dollars which is low cost compared to other controllers. We will also sell) Tj T* (a subscription for lesson content and new firing programs, maybe around ten dollars a month,) Tj T* (but we have not decided yet the exact price. Later we might also sell accessories and other) Tj T* (products and maybe advertising or partnerships. We will sell online through our website and) Tj T* (also to school districts directly. We think many schools will buy it because it is cheap and) Tj T* (the teachers will tell other teachers about it so the sales will grow fast by word of mouth.) Tj T* (The hardware have a good margin and the subscription will make recurring revenue so the) Tj T* (business is scalable. We will figure out the details of the pricing after we talk to more) Tj T* (customers.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj ET
endstream
