BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (There is some competitors who sell kiln controllers but they are not like us. The existing) Tj T* (controllers is expensive, complicated, and made for professional potters not for classrooms.) Tj T* (They dont have education features and are not safe for kids. Some companies also make kilns) Tj T* (with built in controllers but this is more expensive and school must buy whole new kiln.) Tj T* (Because of this we think we have no real competition in the classroom market. Our competitive) Tj T* (advantage is that we are the only one who is focus on students and teachers and make it easy) Tj T* (and educational. Big companies could maybe copy us but we will be first to market and have the) Tj T* (brand. Also we have a website and we are working on getting patent protection for our idea,) Tj T* (which will protect us from competition.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Dashiell Brownleigh is the CEO and is a junior studying business at our university. He is) Tj T* (passionate about education and entrepreneurship and he did a internship once. He lead the team) Tj T* (and do the strategy and sales.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marisol Quentara is the CTO and is a senior studying electrical engineering at our university.) Tj T* (She build the prototype and know about electronics and sensors and programming. She is very) Tj T* (talented.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Tobias Wrenfield is head of product and a sophomore studying art education at our university.) Tj T* (He have experience with ceramics and understand the teachers needs because he took a pottery) Tj T* (class and work in the art department.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are a strong team with business, technology, and art skills together and we work very hard.) Tj T* (We dont have yet a advisor but we are looking for mentors.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have defined our core business concept and we have build a working prototype of the) Tj T* (Kilnbright controller. The prototype can control a small kiln and run a preset program and show) Tj T* (the screen. We also raised some funding, about eight thousand dollars, from family and friends) Tj T* (and a small grant from our university. We have a website also. We have not formed a legal) Tj T* (entity yet but we will do it soon when we need it. We have not sold anything yet and so we have) Tj T* (no revenue at the moment. We have talked to some teachers who said they like the idea, but we) Tj T* (have not done formal customer research yet. For the next year we plan to improve the prototype,) Tj T* (make a bigger version, test in some schools, and start selling. We think we can have revenue of) Tj T* (one million dollars in three years and be profitable soon after, but we dont have a detailed) Tj T* (financial model yet. The cost to make each controller is maybe around eighty dollars but this) Tj T* (is a estimate and could change.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are asking for the prize money from this competition to help us grow Kilnbright. We would) Tj T* (use the money to build more prototypes, pay for safety certification, hire a manufacturer, and) Tj T* (do marketing. We are also asking for mentorship and connections to investors and schools and) Tj T* (any help with legal and business advice. We believe that Kilnbright can be a big success and) Tj T* (make a real impact in education and we are excited to join this competition. Thank you for) Tj T* (considering our application and we hope to be selected so we can take Kilnbright to the next) Tj T* (level and make ceramics safe and fun for every classroom in America.) Tj ET
endstream
